      "id": 1,
      "text": "Stuarts Draft grew when the Shenandoah Valley Railroad began stopping there in 1882, linking it to Roanoke and Hagerstown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stuarts_Draft%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1893, Cohron built the Stuarts Draft Mill beside the tracks, later adding a warehouse that helped local industry thrive.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stuarts_Draft%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Two historic properties in Stuarts Draft are listed on the National Register of Historic Places, including the Colter House, a two‑story brick home on Locust Grove Lane.",
